    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our absolute cornerstone, boasting an elite score of 81.88. His position at the top of the order against a favorable 4.52 xERA arm like Civale creates a perfect storm of plate appearances and scoring potential. **Kyle Tucker** (78.94) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.26) follow closely as high-ceiling plays; **Merrill** benefits immensely from a favorable platoon matchup and an aggressive leadoff spot, while **Tucker** capitalizes on a high-efficiency matchup against Strider. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (73.10) provides high-floor power against a struggling Kochanowicz (5.14 xERA), proving that even with a slight negative dynamic platoon shift, the raw talent and park factors keep him locked into the utility spot.\n\nThe decision to bench **Nolan Schanuel** was the most difficult call of the morning. While he holds a solid 53.01 projection, he ultimately fell short of **Drake Baldwin** and **Coby Mayo** due to our priority on multi-category upside and the specific distribution of opposing pitcher skill today. We are keeping a close watch on **Josh Lowe**, whose score of 57.15 sits just above our marginal threshold. Despite his 9-hole disadvantage, his elite dynamic platoon rating against Yesavage warrants the start over the bench options. We remain cautious of the volatility inherent in our lower-tier starters like **Liam Hicks**, who carries a sub-42 score; however, he retains a roster spot today as we balance our game caps while looking for opportunistic production from the bottom of our lineup.",
